# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Portava — repo-root environment checklist
#
# This file is the INDEX of every secret the project needs and where it is
# provisioned. The two trees keep their own, more detailed examples:
#
#   artifacts/api-server/.env.example      server / worker secrets
#   travel-buddy-standalone/.env.example   Expo client (EXPO_PUBLIC_* only)
#
# Nothing here is loaded automatically — it documents what must exist in the
# Replit deployment secrets and the EAS project environment before a release.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Expo client (local dev) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EAS project environment — required before a store build
# (set via `eas env:create` or the EAS dashboard, NOT in this file)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL          also set per-profile in eas.json
# EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_ORIGIN            also set per-profile in eas.json
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN            client crash reporting
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY          native MapLibre maps
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FOURSQUARE_API_KEY    client-side place lookup
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN                 SECRET — sourcemap upload
#                                   (package.json eas-build-on-success)


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Replit deployment secrets — required in production
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ── Core ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY         SECRET — bypasses RLS; server only
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# SESSION_SECRET                    SECRET — required in production
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS                   CORS allowlist (set in .replit userenv)
#
# ── Error reporting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SENTRY_DSN                        server-side; unset = Sentry disabled
#
# ── Internal job auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# INTERNAL_API_SECRET               SECRET — REQUIRED. POST /internal/
#                                   buddy-requests/expire fails closed (503)
#                                   without it; no SESSION_SECRET fallback.
# COMPASS_TOKEN_SECRET              SECRET
# CLEANUP_ADMIN_SECRET              SECRET
#
# ── Universal / App Links (served by the web-origin server) ──────────────────
# APPLE_APP_ID_PREFIX               Apple Developer Team ID
# ANDROID_CERT_SHA256               signing cert SHA-256 fingerprint(s)
#   Both return 503 until set — a wrong value makes Apple/Google cache a
#   FAILED verification, which is harder to recover from than a retry.
#
# ── Calling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LIVEKIT_URL
# LIVEKIT_API_KEY
# LIVEKIT_API_SECRET                SECRET
#
# ── Third-party data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FOURSQUARE_API_KEY
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY
# MAPBOX_TOKEN
# TICKETMASTER_API_KEY
# AI_INTEGRATIONS_OPENAI_API_KEY    SECRET — stamp art + Compass
# AI_INTEGRATIONS_OPENAI_BASE_URL
#
# ── Optional infrastructure ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REDIS_URL                         backs rate limiting across instances;
#                                   without it limits are per-process only
#
# ── Identity / KYC ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IDENTITY_PROVIDER                 "mock" until a real provider is wired up
